      "content": "Thanks. That's a good start and captures the essence.\n\nHowever, I just ran it through the internal system and the Rigorousness Metric flagged it as \"Low Rigour\" (Score: 3). The partner is actually quite old-school and expects a more comprehensive legal context. \n\nCan you expand the summary slightly? You don't need to change the core message, but please incorporate more of the supporting case law and statutory references mentioned or implied in the judgment to bring that score up. Just make sure they aren't totally random—they should still relate to the development of the duty of care or the maritime framework being discussed.",
